+"""Startup autotuning of the DSpark SPS cost table from real decode steps.
+
+The compact ragged-verify planner prices a decode step as
+``bias + alpha(bs) + theta(M)`` (``SpsAdditiveCostTable``), where ``M`` is the
+verify-token count, rounded up to the captured CUDA graph tier the verify
+forward replays. ``dspark_sps_profiler`` fits that table from the step period
+of real serving rounds; this module does the same measurement inside the
+server, before it reports ready, so a deployment needs no profiling run.
+
+Two halves cooperate:
+
+* Scheduler side (every TP rank, after graph capture): build the cache key from
+  hardware, parallel layout, captured graphs, model and software, agree on it
+  over the TP CPU group, and load a cached table if one exists. Otherwise mark
+  a measurement as pending and describe the cells it needs. The measured table
+  arrives later through ``/set_internal_state``; every rank validates it, the
+  ranks agree, all of them install it and rank 0 caches it.
+* Server side (the HTTP process, in its startup hook, before it listens): for
+  each cell (batch size ``bs``, verify tier ``t``), pin the verify budget so
+  every step verifies exactly ``t`` tokens (the profiler's forced budget),
+  submit ``bs`` synthetic requests, read the scheduler's per-step period
+  records until enough steady steps ran at ``bs`` requests and tier ``t``, and
+  keep their median. Cells run in alternating order over several passes; the
+  per-cell median feeds a robust, monotone fit of the additive tier model.
+
+Any failure leaves every rank on the table it already had; serving starts
+either way.
+"""
+
